still reported all-green because the tests loaded a 6-minute-old `.so`. Added a freshness guard that aborts if the `.so` predates `src/lib.rs`, plus `run_tests.sh` which builds before testing. After the fix, that mutation fails 15 tests — the harness is demonstrably sensitive.\n2. A wrong constant in my own Phase B row 12 (`0xFFFF_FF00 + 0x140` wraps to 64, not `<64`).\n\n### Robustness note on the UB\nThe C shifts by counts ≥ 64 (`val <<= 64 - bits` with `bits == 0`; `val >> bw->bits` with `bw->bits ≥ 64`). The Rust uses `wrapping_shl`/`wrapping_shr`, matching x86-64's `%cl` masking. I verified GCC emits masked `shl`/`shr` at every optimization level and ran the full suite against C references built at **-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os** — all OK, so the match isn't an artifact of the unoptimized reference build.\n\nReproduce with `cd translation && ./run_tests.sh` → `ALL COMBINATIONS PASSED`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the requested `build/` directory was created)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":76514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":941,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3861a91a-657e-4db9-9534-15a2c0ed883b","uuid":"2dc5ad91-09af-48b4-bd2f-31e69216528a","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:47:51.572Z"}
